	<div class="defTop">
		<div class="defDefOf">Definition of </div>
			<div class="defWord">
				<h1>Prime Number</h1>
			</div>
		<div class="defMore"><a href="../prime-composite-number.html"> more ...</a></div>
</div>
<div class="defMid">
<div class="floatRt"><img src="../numbers/images/prime-composite.svg" width="532" height="155" alt="Prime Number"></div>
<div class="defText">
<p>A whole number above 1 that can <b>not</b> be made by multiplying other whole numbers.</p>
<p><b>Example:</b> 5 is a prime number. We cannot multiply 2, 3 or 4 together to make 5. (Only 1&times;5 works but we said to use <b>other</b> whole numbers.)</p>
<p><b>Example:</b> 6 can be made by 2 &times; 3 so is NOT a prime number (it is a composite number).</p>
<p>All whole numbers above 1 are either composite or prime.<br>
</p>
</div>
